@Mica-r7g

I understand your point, but “compromise from both sides” doesn’t mean the situations are symmetrical. Egypt changing how it gets water has no effect on Ethiopia. Ethiopia’s operation of a massive upstream dam can affect water reaching Egypt and Sudan, particularly during prolonged droughts.

Ethiopia absolutely has a right to develop and generate electricity. The issue is whether the dam is operated under agreed rules that balance Ethiopia’s right to equitable use with the downstream countries’ protection from significant harm. That’s literally why the dispute has centred on filling, drought management and binding operating rules not on whether Ethiopia is allowed to develop at all.
